# GiftImportService Implementation

This implementation stages one `npsp__DataImport__c` record per gift, inserts them with partial-success handling (so a bad row at the insert stage doesn't block the rest), processes them synchronously through NPSP's `BDI_DataImport_API` using the org's configured Data Import settings, then re-queries the processed rows (NPSP's own writes are the source of truth) to build the results in the original input order.

File: force-app/main/default/classes/GiftImportService.cls
```apex
/**
 * Routes one-off website gifts through NPSP's Data Import / BDI engine instead of
 * inserting Contacts and Opportunities directly, so NPSP's contact matching, household
 * creation and donation processing rules apply - and so each staged npsp__DataImport__c
 * record remains in the org as an audit trail of what was imported.
 */
public class GiftImportService {

    public class WebGift {
        public String firstName;
        public String lastName;
        public String email;        // the donor's personal email
        public Decimal amount;
        public Date giftDate;
    }

    public class ImportResult {
        public Boolean success;
        public Id contactId;        // the matched or created contact
        public Id opportunityId;    // the created donation
        public String errorMessage; // NPSP's failure information when success is false
    }

    public static List<ImportResult> importGifts(List<WebGift> gifts) {
        List<ImportResult> results = new List<ImportResult>();

        if (gifts == null || gifts.isEmpty()) {
            return results;
        }

        // Build one staging record per gift, preserving input order.
        List<npsp__DataImport__c> dataImports = new List<npsp__DataImport__c>();
        for (WebGift gift : gifts) {
            npsp__DataImport__c di = new npsp__DataImport__c();
            di.npsp__Contact1_Firstname__c = gift.firstName;
            di.npsp__Contact1_Lastname__c = gift.lastName;
            di.npsp__Contact1_Personal_Email__c = gift.email;
            di.npsp__Donation_Amount__c = gift.amount;
            di.npsp__Donation_Date__c = gift.giftDate;
            di.npsp__Donation_Donor__c = 'Contact1';
            dataImports.add(di);
        }

        // Insert with partial success so one bad row can't block the whole batch.
        Database.SaveResult[] saveResults = Database.insert(dataImports, false);

        // Track, per original index: the Data Import Id (if insert succeeded) or the
        // insert-time error message (if it didn't).
        Id[] dataImportIdByIndex = new Id[dataImports.size()];
        String[] insertErrorByIndex = new String[dataImports.size()];
        List<npsp__DataImport__c> toProcess = new List<npsp__DataImport__c>();

        for (Integer i = 0; i < saveResults.size(); i++) {
            Database.SaveResult sr = saveResults[i];
            if (sr.isSuccess()) {
                dataImportIdByIndex[i] = dataImports[i].Id;
                toProcess.add(dataImports[i]);
            } else {
                insertErrorByIndex[i] = sr.getErrors().isEmpty()
                    ? 'Unable to stage gift for import.'
                    : sr.getErrors()[0].getMessage();
            }
        }

        // Process the successfully staged rows synchronously through NPSP's BDI engine,
        // using the org's configured Data Import settings (matching rules, donation
        // matching behaviour, etc. as set up in npsp__Data_Import_Settings__c).
        if (!toProcess.isEmpty()) {
            npsp.Data_Import_Settings__c diSettings = npsp.UTIL_CustomSettingsFacade.getDataImportSettings();
            npsp.BDI_DataImport_API.processDataImportRecords(diSettings, toProcess, false);
        }

        // Re-query to read back NPSP's authoritative results rather than relying on
        // in-memory state after the BDI call.
        Map<Id, npsp__DataImport__c> processedById = new Map<Id, npsp__DataImport__c>();
        if (!toProcess.isEmpty()) {
            Set<Id> ids = new Set<Id>();
            for (npsp__DataImport__c di : toProcess) {
                ids.add(di.Id);
            }
            processedById = new Map<Id, npsp__DataImport__c>([
                SELECT Id, npsp__Status__c, npsp__Contact1Imported__c,
                       npsp__DonationImported__c, npsp__FailureInformation__c
                FROM npsp__DataImport__c
                WHERE Id IN :ids
            ]);
        }

        // Rebuild results in the original input order.
        for (Integer i = 0; i < gifts.size(); i++) {
            ImportResult result = new ImportResult();
            Id diId = dataImportIdByIndex[i];

            if (diId == null) {
                result.success = false;
                result.errorMessage = insertErrorByIndex[i];
            } else {
                npsp__DataImport__c processed = processedById.get(diId);
                if (processed == null) {
                    result.success = false;
                    result.errorMessage = 'Data Import record could not be retrieved after processing.';
                } else {
                    result.success = (processed.npsp__Status__c == 'Imported');
                    result.contactId = processed.npsp__Contact1Imported__c;
                    result.opportunityId = processed.npsp__DonationImported__c;
                    result.errorMessage = processed.npsp__FailureInformation__c;
                }
            }

            results.add(result);
        }

        return results;
    }
}
```

**Key design notes:**

- **Audit trail**: `npsp__DataImport__c` records are inserted (never deleted), satisfying the requirement that staged records remain as the audit trail.
- **Bulk safety**: a single `Database.insert(..., false)` and a single `processDataImportRecords` call handle all 200 gifts in one pass; one failed insert doesn't block others (`allOrNone=false`), and NPSP's BDI engine itself processes each row independently, writing `Failed`/`Imported` status per row without throwing for the whole batch.
- **Synchronous processing**: `npsp.BDI_DataImport_API.processDataImportRecords(diSettings, toProcess, false)` runs BDI inline in the same transaction (`isDryRun = false`), using `npsp.UTIL_CustomSettingsFacade.getDataImportSettings()` to pick up the org's actual Data Import settings (contact matching rules, donation matching behavior, etc.) rather than hardcoding behavior.
- **Order preservation**: results are assembled by walking the original `gifts` list via a parallel `dataImportIdByIndex` array, so order is guaranteed regardless of DML/query reordering.
- **Failure reporting**: `errorMessage` surfaces either the insert-time DML error (rare, e.g., validation rule) or NPSP's own `npsp__FailureInformation__c`, matching the "NPSP's failure information" requirement.
- **Null/empty input**: returns an empty list immediately.

